    <briefdescription>
<para>Guidelines for high-churn scenario behavior. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><bold>Definition:</bold> High churn = &gt;100 model updates/sec or &gt;1000 concurrent links/sec</para>
<para><bold>Expected Performance Envelope:</bold><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Model serialization: 5-50 ms (independent of churn)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Link creation: 1-10 ms per link (scales with contention)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Conflict probability: 5-15% under &gt;500 concurrent operations</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>No silent failures; all conflicts explicitly reported </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
